<article class="env-lemma" id="0FUH">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FUH">Lemma <span data-tag="0FUH">50.10.4</span>.</a> With notation as above we have </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\Omega ^ p_{L^\star /S, n} = \Omega ^ p_{L^\star /S, 0} \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ X} \mathcal{L}^{\otimes n}$ for all $n \in \mathbf{Z}$ as quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\Omega ^\bullet _{X/S} = \Omega ^\bullet _{L/X, 0}$ as complexes, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for $n > 0$ and $p \geq 0$ we have $\Omega ^ p_{L/X, n} = \Omega ^ p_{L^\star /S, n}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      In each case there is a globally defined canonical map which is an isomorphism by local calculations which we omit. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>